container-all-solid — alternate diagonal on a coplanar patch:
Of 8164 canonical triangles, 8162 match exactly. Both renders have identical
facet count, bbox and signed volume. Both quads have this exact vertex set:
A = (54.87410354614258, -144.10888671875, 0)
B = (54.915061950683594, -144.199951171875, 0.00000019073486612342094)
C = (54.91508102416992, -144.1999969482422, 0)
D = (54.91508102416992, -144.1999969482422, 0.00000019073486612342094)
Worker quad: A-B-D plus A-C-D (diagonal A-D).
Mayor quad: B-C-D plus A-B-C (diagonal B-C).
Every unmatched vertex has an exact counterpart in the other mesh (delta 0).
The patch lies within a 1.90735e-7 mm slab about Z=0, below REV 3c's 1e-4 mm
vertex tolerance. Best triangle-to-triangle vertex deltas are 1.90735e-7
and 4.57764e-5 mm; this is specifically the alternate-diagonal case accepted
by the mayor in REV 3c, rather than a blanket triangle-comparison waiver.

